 "notes": "Observed power-constrained 95% upper limit on the DM lifetime traced from the black curve of Fig. S7 (plots/Lifetime_Limits.pdf, vector paths; axes calibrated from tick labels). Fig. S7 gives tau for decay to a single photon of energy m/2; per the paper, for axion-like DM decaying to two photons the lifetime limit is twice as strong, so tau_a = 2*tau was used. Converted to the axion-photon coupling via Gamma(a->gamma gamma) = g_agamma^2 m_a^3/(64 pi) = 1/tau_a, i.e. g = sqrt(64 pi/(m_a^3 tau_a)). Mass axis: m_a = m_chi from 5 to 16 keV (5e3-1.6e4 eV). Fiducial DM model: conservative uncontracted NFW (rho_0=6.6e6 Msun/kpc^3, r_s=19.1 kpc), local density 0.29 GeV/cm^3; Milky Way halo D-factor limit, scales linearly with assumed density. Green smooth curve (median expected) and 1/2-sigma bands not reported. Curve is jagged (masked instrumental-line windows); 100 points linearly interpolated in mass.",
